  "caption": "Quinn booked a snow trip six weeks out. Last trip, day 3 at 3pm, the legs turned to jelly.\n\nKay's take: it's not all bad luck. Skiers more often hurt knees and snowboarders wrists, and injuries cluster in afternoons and around day 3, when legs are tired.\n\nWhat can help: six weeks of leg endurance work twice a week (squats, split squats, step-downs), slow lowering, single-leg balance and landing practice, wrist guards and a helmet, a lesson to learn falling and speed control, and warming up, taking breaks and stopping early when legs tire.\n\nGet it checked after a twisting fall with a pop, rapid swelling, or a knee that won't take weight or feels unstable.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
